1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,512
I am writing this on a computer in my
college library, and I

2
00:00:03,532 --> 00:00:07,285
think I am being watched from the dark
between the shelves.

3
00:00:07,305 --> 00:00:08,974
I know how that sounds.

4
00:00:08,994 --> 00:00:13,008
But my best friend trusted the wrong
person, and now he is gone.

5
00:00:13,028 --> 00:00:15,313
If you read nothing else, read this.

6
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:17,054
Let me take you back to the beginning.

7
00:00:17,654 --> 00:00:20,181
Last year I met a guy named Jack.

8
00:00:20,201 --> 00:00:24,572
We liked the same games, the same films,
even the same dumb jokes.

9
00:00:24,592 --> 00:00:27,968
For the first time at that school, I had a
real friend.

10
00:00:27,988 --> 00:00:30,891
We played online almost every night after
class.

11
00:00:31,491 --> 00:00:36,010
Then, last winter, Jack started seeing a
girl from one of our classes.

12
00:00:36,030 --> 00:00:37,601
Her name was Elisa.

13
00:00:37,621 --> 00:00:41,500
At first she seemed kind, and I was
honestly happy for him.

14
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:44,214
But a month in, Jack began to pull away.

15
00:00:44,234 --> 00:00:45,722
He stopped answering.

16
00:00:45,742 --> 00:00:47,415
He only wanted to be with her.

17
00:00:48,015 --> 00:00:51,096
One morning we were waiting in the
cafeteria line.

18
00:00:51,116 --> 00:00:54,094
I made a small joke, and Jack turned on
me.

19
00:00:54,114 --> 00:00:56,829
"This line is too long. I need to get out
of here."

20
00:00:56,849 --> 00:00:59,058
He shouted at a girl behind us.

21
00:00:59,078 --> 00:01:01,159
Then he just ran out of the building.

22
00:01:01,179 --> 00:01:02,531
That was not my friend.

23
00:01:03,131 --> 00:01:05,427
After that he stopped coming to class.

24
00:01:05,447 --> 00:01:09,941
One evening I passed Elisa in the hall and
asked if Jack was okay.

25
00:01:09,961 --> 00:01:12,846
She smiled at me, and the smile was wrong.

26
00:01:12,866 --> 00:01:14,342
"He is better than ever."

27
00:01:14,362 --> 00:01:17,829
She said each word slowly, like a warning,
and walked away.

28
00:01:18,429 --> 00:01:21,131
That night I called him, expecting
nothing.

29
00:01:21,151 --> 00:01:22,645
He picked up at once.

30
00:01:22,665 --> 00:01:27,088
His voice was low and shaking, like a man
trying to get out of a trap.

31
00:01:27,108 --> 00:01:29,327
I told him I was coming over.

32
00:01:29,347 --> 00:01:33,905
Forty minutes later he was at my door, and
I knew something was badly wrong.

33
00:01:34,505 --> 00:01:38,110
I let him in and turned off the lights
because he begged me to.

34
00:01:38,130 --> 00:01:40,768
In the dark he was crying, but the tears
were

35
00:01:40,788 --> 00:01:43,313
black, like ink running down his face.

36
00:01:43,333 --> 00:01:46,894
"She did this to me. She caught me crying
this stuff and said I was ready."

37
00:01:46,914 --> 00:01:48,709
Ready for what, he did not know.

38
00:01:49,309 --> 00:01:51,356
Then a soft knock came at the door.

39
00:01:51,376 --> 00:01:53,406
A girl's voice, calm and sweet.

40
00:01:53,426 --> 00:01:57,415
"Jackie, I know you are in there. It is
time. They are waiting for us."

41
00:01:57,435 --> 00:02:00,130
Jack jumped up, ran out the back, and
vanished

42
00:02:00,150 --> 00:02:02,437
into the woods behind my building.

43
00:02:02,457 --> 00:02:05,177
I called the police and chased after him.

44
00:02:05,197 --> 00:02:08,390
Something hit the back of my head, and the
world went black.

45
00:02:08,990 --> 00:02:10,683
I woke tied to a tree.

46
00:02:10,703 --> 00:02:13,709
In a clearing in front of me stood a ring
of figures

47
00:02:13,729 --> 00:02:16,337
in long black robes and pale blue masks.

48
00:02:16,357 --> 00:02:18,969
In the middle, strapped to a chair, was
Jack.

49
00:02:18,989 --> 00:02:20,779
One of them lifted her mask.

50
00:02:20,799 --> 00:02:22,073
It was Elisa.

51
00:02:22,093 --> 00:02:25,732
A taller one opened an old black book and
began to read.

52
00:02:26,332 --> 00:02:29,259
As the voice read, the ground began to
shake.

53
00:02:29,279 --> 00:02:33,927
Black tendrils rose from the frost like
weeds and wrapped around Jack's chair.

54
00:02:33,947 --> 00:02:36,616
They pressed a cracked blue mask over his
face.

55
00:02:36,636 --> 00:02:39,971
Where his eyes had been, only black tar
ran down.

56
00:02:39,991 --> 00:02:42,580
He was still alive, and I could not look
away.

57
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:45,261
Then, far off, I heard sirens.

58
00:02:45,281 --> 00:02:46,624
The reader stopped.

59
00:02:46,644 --> 00:02:49,881
In the sudden quiet, a low laugh came from
the chair.

60
00:02:49,901 --> 00:02:51,305
"You made him mad."

61
00:02:51,325 --> 00:02:55,782
The thing wearing my friend tore free of
its straps and turned on the circle.

62
00:02:55,802 --> 00:02:58,177
I will not describe what I heard next.

63
00:02:58,197 --> 00:03:02,324
The frost went red, and the robed figures
stopped screaming one by one.

64
00:03:02,924 --> 00:03:07,260
I woke to a flashlight in my face and an
officer shouting for help.

65
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,612
They got me out.

66
00:03:08,632 --> 00:03:13,435
At the hospital they told me I would live,
but one of my kidneys was gone.

67
00:03:13,455 --> 00:03:14,885
A year has passed.

68
00:03:14,905 --> 00:03:19,319
Jack is still missing, blamed for ten
deaths and one attempted murder.

69
00:03:19,339 --> 00:03:20,317
Mine.

70
00:03:20,337 --> 00:03:24,317
This video is inspired by the story You
Can't Trust Everyone,

71
00:03:24,337 --> 00:03:27,653
as published on an online horror story
page.

72
00:03:27,673 --> 00:03:28,842
So tell me.

73
00:03:28,862 --> 00:03:30,067
Who would you have trusted?

